+## K230 VGLite renderer
+
+* *TDVP_VGLITE_FRAME_TIMING*: set to a non-zero value to log the time spent
+  in `vg_lite_finish()` for each output render pass.
+* *TDVP_VGLITE_DIAGNOSTICS*: set to `1` for a short, controlled reproduction
+  of a presentation issue. It emits `TDVP_VGLITE_DIAG` records for VGLite
+  texture uploads (damage rectangle count, copied bytes, and complete source
+  texture bytes), completion, DRM commit submission, FB queueing, and page-flip
+  completion. The completion record also contains texture/solid clip-rectangle
+  and VGLite-blit-attempt counts, so damage fragmentation can be correlated
+  with `vg_lite_finish()` latency without coalescing clips unsafely. The common
+  `wlr_buffer` pointer and DRM FB ID correlate the
+  presentation records; texture logs quantify the SHM upload/cache-maintenance
+  tradeoff. It is off by default and intentionally produces records at the
+  texture-update and output-frame rates; do not leave it enabled during normal
+  use.
+
 ## Headless backend
 
